# Line endings are normalised in the repository and checked out as LF everywhere.
#
# Not cosmetic. Three things break without this, and the first one already did:
#
#   1. `rustfmt.toml` sets `newline_style = "Unix"`, so a CRLF checkout makes
#      `cargo fmt --check` fail on every Rust file. The Windows CI job failed exactly this way
#      on the first push, with 21 "Incorrect newline style" errors.
#   2. `crates/protocol/tests/live/*.sh` will not execute with CRLF line endings.
#   3. The golden byte fixtures must never be touched by text normalisation at all.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit for the files where it is load-bearing.
*.rs      text eol=lf
*.toml    text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf diff=bash
*.capnp   text eol=lf
*.pem     text eol=lf

# Binary. `-text` disables every form of normalisation, so a Windows checkout cannot corrupt
# a fixture whose whole purpose is being byte-exact (crates/protocol/tests/fixtures/README.md).
*.bin     -text
*.png     -text
*.ico     -text
*.woff2   -text
*.webp    -text

# Generated, and reviewed by diffing rather than by reading. Marked so GitHub collapses them
# in a pull request without hiding them from `git diff`.
schema/*.json                     linguist-generated=true
crates/contract/src/generated.rs  linguist-generated=true
docs/ERRORS.md                    linguist-generated=true
pnpm-lock.yaml                    linguist-generated=true

# The UI mockup exported from Claude Design (docs/mockup/README.md). Vendored, not authored here:
# marked so it stays out of GitHub's language statistics — a megabyte of design export would
# otherwise report this as an HTML repository — and collapses in a pull request. `.thumbnail` is a
# WebP with no extension, so `text=auto` has to be told to keep its hands off.
docs/mockup/**                    linguist-vendored=true
docs/mockup/.thumbnail            -text
